    "result_text": "The full test suite passes with `BUILD SUCCESS`.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the email-uniqueness rule for owner creation, following the existing duplicate-telephone pattern in the codebase:\n\n1. **`DuplicateEmailException`** (new) \u2014 a `RuntimeException` in the `rest.validation` package, mirroring `DuplicateTelephoneException`.\n\n2. **`OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner`** \u2014 after normalizing the e-mail (which lower-cases it via `EmailNormalizer`), it now checks whether the normalized address is already used by any existing owner and, if so, throws `DuplicateEmailException`. The check guards against `null` (the e-mail field is optional) and compares case-insensitively so only owners with a matching lower-cased e-mail collide.\n\n3. **`ExceptionControllerAdvice`** \u2014 added an `@ExceptionHandler` for `DuplicateEmailException` that returns **409 Conflict**, consistent with the existing duplicate-telephone/household handlers.\n\nThe new acceptance test `coreRejectsDuplicateEmail` passes, and the full suite is green.",
