        "findings": "VERDICT: LGTM\n\nThe change slots cleanly into the codebase's established conventions:\n\n- `DuplicateEmailException` is a direct sibling of `DuplicateTelephoneException` in the same `validation` package, with the same shape and a doc comment that matches the existing style.\n- The exception handler in `ExceptionControllerAdvice` mirrors the neighboring `handleDuplicateHouseholdException` / telephone handlers exactly (same logging, `detailBuild`, 409 status), so it reads as one more entry in an existing family rather than a new pattern.\n- The uniqueness check in `addOwner` is placed right alongside the pre-existing `telephoneInUse` check and follows the same idiom (stream over `findAllOwners()`, throw on match). A maintainer would find it natural precisely because it copies the adjacent telephone logic.\n- The `String email = ...; owner.setEmail(email)` refactor is the minimal, sensible way to reuse the normalized value for the comparison.\n\nNothing is duplicated inappropriately and no class is becoming a catch-all \u2014 `ExceptionControllerAdvice` is already the designated home for these translations. The structure is consistent and additive.\n\n(One non-structural note, outside this review's scope: the check now triggers a second `findAllOwners()` fetch in the same method, but that mirrors the existing telephone approach and is a correctness/efficiency matter rather than a structural one.)"
